  "protocol": "luanti_addressed_balanced_object_token_dqn_v2: real repaired seven-channel Luanti addressed balanced retrieval; reward-only off-policy DQN from 11x11 public vision, previous chosen action, previous scalar reward, and public adjacent-wall legal-action masks only. The counterbalanced course nulls the identity->side frequency shortcut (each identity left/right 50/50 and each identity queried equally per contiguous seed window), so chance-level no-memory success at 0.50 is the guaranteed bound and only real delayed retrieval can exceed it. Predeclared budget escalation: 1,024 training worlds from 16,000,000 and 32 held-out worlds from 16,002,000 under the same gates. Every model includes the same object-token visual event encoder and its parameters count toward capacity matching; only full PLWM writes four first-frame public object tokens and retrieves with the delayed public query. No cue/query labels, coordinates, symbolic bridge state, seed, teacher trajectory, external planner, shaped reward, or PLWM-only input. This is one CUDA smoke, never an architecture claim.",
